    <worksheet name='% Active SKU above benchmark per Country'>
      <layout-options>
        <title>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontcolor='#e15759'>&lt;Sheet Name&gt;</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#499894' fontsize='10'>Please note: </run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#499894' fontsize='10'>The &quot;Benchmark&quot; is pre-calculated across the entire available range of Order Dates from the database (e.g. 1 May to 31 July). </run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#499894' fontsize='10'>Then, in the fltered range of the Order Dates  (e.g. 1 June to 1 July), when any SKU&apos;s latest listed price is above the &quot;Benchmark&quot; (having a markup),  the SKU is counted in the &quot;% Active SKU above benchmark&quot; in this chart. Therefore, when the filter of the Order Dates is adjusted, the chart is updated on-the-fly.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </title>
      </layout-options>
      <table>
        <view>
          <datasources />
          <datasource-dependencies datasource='federated.0svw0ya0k72xbm10bcz401tz7j0v'>
            <column datatype='string' name='[City]' role='dimension' semantic-role='[City].[Name]' type='nominal' />
            <column-instance column='[City]' derivation='None' name='[none:City:nk]' pivot='key' type='nominal' />
          </datasource-dependencies>
          <aggregation value='true' />
        </view>
        <style>
          <style-rule element='cell'>
            <format attr='width' field='[federated.0svw0ya0k72xbm10bcz401tz7j0v].[none:Country_Name:nk]' value='92' />
          </style-rule>
          <style-rule element='label'>
            <format attr='font-weight' field='[federated.0svw0ya0k72xbm10bcz401tz7j0v].[none:Country_Name:nk]' value='bold' />
          </style-rule>
          <style-rule element='table'>
            <format attr='background-color' value='#f5f5f5' />
          </style-rule>
          <style-rule element='title'>
            <format attr='background-color' value='#f5f5f5' />
          </style-rule>
        </style>
        <panes>
          <pane selection-relaxation-option='selection-relaxation-allow'>
